# knag — non-secret defaults. Copy to .env (this file is committed; .env is not).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Secrets go in two places, never here:
#   - Cloudflare Worker secrets, via `wrangler secret put`:
#       KNAG_PASSPHRASE      PWA login          (different per environment)
#       KNAG_BEARER_TOKEN    agent / MCP        (different per environment)
#   - .env.local (gitignored), for credentials that stay on this machine:
#       CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN  the DEV account token. Never the prod one — prod
#                             lives only in the GitHub Environment (ADR-002).
#       GH_TOKEN              github identity for ghw

# Host that `make health` and `make verify` check.
HOST=knag.danjamkuhn.com

# 🔴 Which Cloudflare account each environment is allowed to touch.
#
# `make deploy` and `make migrate` refuse to run unless the ACTIVE credential
# resolves to the id below. This is not belt-and-braces — wrangler also honours a
# machine-global `wrangler login` stored outside this repo, which no project
# setting overrides. Without the assertion, a stale login silently decides where
# your deploy lands. See scripts/preflight.sh.
#
# Read an id with: pnpm exec wrangler whoami
CF_ACCOUNT_ID_DEV=9138ff69256d01d60787fbbe9a73b7d8
CF_ACCOUNT_ID_PROD=
